
# CodeAlpha Hangman Game

## Project Description
This is a simple text-based Hangman game developed
in Python as part of the CodeAlpha Python Programming
Internship.

The player must guess a hidden word one letter at a
time before making six incorrect guesses.

## Features
- Five predefined words
- Random word selection
- One-letter guessing
- Maximum of six incorrect guesses
- Input validation
- Repeated-guess detection
- Win and lose messages

## Technologies Used
- Python
- random module
- Lists and strings
- While and for loops
- Conditional statements
- User input and output

## How to Run
1. Install Python 3 if it is not already installed.
2. Download or clone this repository.
3. Open the project folder in PyCharm.
4. Run hangman.py.

No external Python libraries are required.

## Files
- hangman.py: Main game program
